## WINDOW

Opens, closes, and manages Workbench windows.

Syntax: WINDOW WINDOWS/M/A [OPEN/S] [CLOSE/S] [SNAPSHOT/S] [ACTIVATE/S]
               [MIN/S] [MAX/S] [FRONT/S] [BACK/S] [CYCLE/K]

Parameters:
  WINDOWS/M/A    Window names (required, multiple allowed)
                 Values: ROOT (main Workbench window) or absolute paths
                 e.g. "Work:", "SYS:Utilities", "RAM:"
  OPEN/S         Open the window
  CLOSE/S        Close the window
  SNAPSHOT/S     Save window position and size
  ACTIVATE/S     Make the window active
  MIN/S          Minimize to smallest size
  MAX/S          Maximize to largest size
  FRONT/S        Bring to front
  BACK/S         Send to back
  CYCLE/K        Cycle through windows
                 Values: PREVIOUS, NEXT

Multiple switches can be combined in one command.

Examples:
  'WINDOW "Work:" OPEN'
  'WINDOW "Work:" FRONT ACTIVATE'
  'WINDOW root SNAPSHOT'
  'WINDOW "SYS:Utilities" CLOSE'
  'WINDOW "Work:" OPEN FRONT ACTIVATE'

## ACTIVATEWINDOW

Makes a window the active (focused) one.

Syntax: ACTIVATEWINDOW [WINDOW]

Parameters:
  WINDOW    Window path or ROOT (default: active window)

Examples:
  'ACTIVATEWINDOW "Work:"'
  'ACTIVATEWINDOW root'

## CHANGEWINDOW

Changes position and size of a window simultaneously.

Syntax: CHANGEWINDOW [WINDOW] [LEFTEDGE/N] [TOPEDGE/N] [WIDTH/N] [HEIGHT/N]

Parameters:
  WINDOW       Window path or ROOT
  LEFTEDGE/N   New left edge position in pixels
  TOPEDGE/N    New top edge position in pixels
  WIDTH/N      New width in pixels
  HEIGHT/N     New height in pixels

Examples:
  'CHANGEWINDOW root LEFTEDGE 10 TOPEDGE 30 WIDTH 400 HEIGHT 300'
  'CHANGEWINDOW "Work:" LEFTEDGE 50 TOPEDGE 50 WIDTH 500 HEIGHT 400'

## MOVEWINDOW

Moves a window to a new position.

Syntax: MOVEWINDOW [WINDOW] [LEFTEDGE/N] [TOPEDGE/N]

Parameters:
  WINDOW       Window path or ROOT
  LEFTEDGE/N   New left edge position in pixels
  TOPEDGE/N    New top edge position in pixels

Examples:
  'MOVEWINDOW root LEFTEDGE 0 TOPEDGE 0'
  'MOVEWINDOW "Work:" LEFTEDGE 100 TOPEDGE 50'

## SIZEWINDOW

Resizes a window.

Syntax: SIZEWINDOW [WINDOW] [WIDTH/N] [HEIGHT/N]

Parameters:
  WINDOW     Window path or ROOT
  WIDTH/N    New width in pixels
  HEIGHT/N   New height in pixels

Examples:
  'SIZEWINDOW root WIDTH 640 HEIGHT 480'
  'SIZEWINDOW "Work:" WIDTH 300 HEIGHT 200'

## WINDOWTOFRONT

Brings a window to the front.

Syntax: WINDOWTOFRONT [WINDOW]

Parameters:
  WINDOW    Window path or ROOT

Examples:
  'WINDOWTOFRONT root'
  'WINDOWTOFRONT "Work:"'

## WINDOWTOBACK

Sends a window to the back.

Syntax: WINDOWTOBACK [WINDOW]

Parameters:
  WINDOW    Window path or ROOT

Examples:
  'WINDOWTOBACK root'
  'WINDOWTOBACK "Work:"'

## ZOOMWINDOW

Toggles window to its alternative (zoomed) size. The alternative size
is typically the minimum size or a previously saved zoom position.

Syntax: ZOOMWINDOW [WINDOW]

Parameters:
  WINDOW    Window path or ROOT

Example:
  'ZOOMWINDOW "Work:"'

## UNZOOMWINDOW

Restores a window from its zoomed (alternative) size to normal.

Syntax: UNZOOMWINDOW [WINDOW]

Parameters:
  WINDOW    Window path or ROOT

Example:
  'UNZOOMWINDOW "Work:"'

## VIEW

Scrolls the visible area of a window.

Syntax: VIEW [WINDOW] [PAGE/S] [PIXEL/S] [UP/S] [DOWN/S] [LEFT/S] [RIGHT/S]

Parameters:
  WINDOW     Window path or ROOT
  PAGE/S     Scroll by one page
  PIXEL/S    Scroll by one pixel
  UP/S       Scroll up
  DOWN/S     Scroll down
  LEFT/S     Scroll left
  RIGHT/S    Scroll right

If neither PAGE nor PIXEL is specified, scrolls by one line.
Direction switches can be combined.

Examples:
  'VIEW root PAGE DOWN'
  'VIEW "Work:" PIXEL RIGHT'
  'VIEW root UP LEFT'

## LOCKGUI

Locks the user interface. All drawer windows are disabled.
Calls are nested — each LOCKGUI requires a matching UNLOCKGUI.

Syntax: LOCKGUI

Example:
  'LOCKGUI'
  /* ... batch operations ... */
  'UNLOCKGUI'

## UNLOCKGUI

Unlocks the user interface after a LOCKGUI call.
Must be called once for each LOCKGUI.

Syntax: UNLOCKGUI

Example:
  'UNLOCKGUI'

## ICON

Manipulates icons in a window. Supports selecting, moving, opening,
and navigating icons.

Syntax: ICON [WINDOW] NAMES/M [OPEN/S] [MAKEVISIBLE/S] [SELECT/S] [UNSELECT/S]
             [UP/N] [DOWN/N] [LEFT/N] [RIGHT/N] [X/N] [Y/N]
             [ACTIVATE/K] [CYCLE/K] [MOVE/K]

Parameters:
  WINDOW         Window path or ROOT
  NAMES/M        Icon names (multiple allowed)
  OPEN/S         Open icon (launch program or open drawer)
  MAKEVISIBLE/S  Scroll window to make icon visible
  SELECT/S       Select icon
  UNSELECT/S     Deselect icon
  UP/N           Move icon up by N pixels
  DOWN/N         Move icon down by N pixels
  LEFT/N         Move icon left by N pixels
  RIGHT/N        Move icon right by N pixels
  X/N            Set icon to absolute X position
  Y/N            Set icon to absolute Y position
  ACTIVATE/K     Activate neighboring icon
                 Values: UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT
  CYCLE/K        Cycle through icons
                 Values: PREVIOUS, NEXT
  MOVE/K         Navigate drawer hierarchy
                 Values: IN (enter drawer), OUT (go to parent)

Examples:
  /* Select icons */
  'ICON WINDOW root NAMES Workbench Work SELECT'

  /* Move icon to absolute position */
  'ICON WINDOW "Work:" NAMES "MyProgram" X 100 Y 50'

  /* Open icon (launch program) */
  'ICON WINDOW "SYS:Utilities" NAMES MultiView OPEN'

  /* Make icon visible */
  'ICON WINDOW root NAMES "HiddenIcon" MAKEVISIBLE'

  /* Move icon relative */
  'ICON WINDOW root NAMES "MyIcon" RIGHT 20 DOWN 10'

## INFO

Opens the information dialog for a file, drawer, or volume.

Syntax: INFO NAME/A

Parameters:
  NAME/A    Absolute path of the object (required)

Examples:
  'INFO NAME "SYS:"'
  'INFO NAME "Work:MyFile"'

## NEWDRAWER

Creates a new drawer (directory).

Syntax: NEWDRAWER NAME/A

Parameters:
  NAME/A    Absolute path of the new drawer (required)

Examples:
  'NEWDRAWER "RAM:NewDrawer"'
  'NEWDRAWER "Work:Projects/New"'

## DELETE

Deletes files or drawers.

Syntax: DELETE NAME/A [ALL/S]

Parameters:
  NAME/A    Absolute path of the file or drawer (required)
  ALL/S     Delete contents recursively (for drawers)

Note: Without ALL, non-empty drawers cannot be deleted.

Examples:
  'DELETE "RAM:TempFile"'
  'DELETE "RAM:TempFolder" ALL'

## RENAME

Renames a file, drawer, or volume.

Syntax: RENAME OLDNAME/A NEWNAME/A

Parameters:
  OLDNAME/A    Absolute path of the object (required)
  NEWNAME/A    New name only, without path (required)

Note: NEWNAME is just the new name, not a full path. The object stays
in the same directory.

Examples:
  'RENAME "RAM:OldName" "NewName"'
  'RENAME "Work:readme.txt" "README.txt"'

## GETATTR

Queries information from the Workbench database. Returns the value
in RESULT (requires OPTIONS RESULTS).

Syntax: GETATTR OBJECT/A [NAME/K] [STEM/K] [VAR/K]

Parameters:
  OBJECT/A   The attribute to query (required)
  NAME/K     Context for the query (e.g. window path for WINDOW.* objects)
  STEM/K     Store result in a stem variable
  VAR/K      Store result in a named variable

Queryable Objects:

Application info:
  APPLICATION.VERSION      Workbench version string
  APPLICATION.SCREEN       Screen name
  APPLICATION.AREXX        ARexx port name
  APPLICATION.LASTERROR    Last error message

Font info:
  APPLICATION.FONT.SCREEN.NAME|SIZE    Screen font
  APPLICATION.FONT.ICON.NAME|SIZE      Icon font
  APPLICATION.FONT.SYSTEM.NAME|SIZE    System font

Icon border:
  APPLICATION.ICONBORDER.LEFT|TOP|RIGHT|BOTTOM

Window list:
  WINDOWS.COUNT            Number of open windows
  WINDOWS.ACTIVE           Path of the active window
  WINDOWS.0 ... WINDOWS.N  Path of the Nth window

Window details (use NAME=path):
  WINDOW.LEFT|TOP          Window position
  WINDOW.WIDTH|HEIGHT      Window size
  WINDOW.MIN.WIDTH|HEIGHT  Minimum size
  WINDOW.MAX.WIDTH|HEIGHT  Maximum size
  WINDOW.VIEW.LEFT|TOP     Scroll position
  WINDOW.SCREEN.NAME|WIDTH|HEIGHT  Screen info

Icon info (use NAME=window path):
  WINDOW.ICONS.ALL.COUNT               Total icon count
  WINDOW.ICONS.SELECTED.COUNT           Selected icon count
  WINDOW.ICONS.UNSELECTED.COUNT         Unselected icon count
  WINDOW.ICONS.ALL.n.NAME|LEFT|TOP|WIDTH|HEIGHT|TYPE|STATUS
  WINDOW.ICONS.SELECTED.n.NAME|LEFT|TOP|WIDTH|HEIGHT|TYPE|STATUS
  WINDOW.ICONS.UNSELECTED.n.NAME|LEFT|TOP|WIDTH|HEIGHT|TYPE|STATUS

Icon TYPE values: DISK, DRAWER, TOOL, PROJECT, GARBAGE, DEVICE, KICK, APPICON

Examples:
  OPTIONS RESULTS

  /* Workbench version */
  'GETATTR APPLICATION.VERSION'
  SAY "Version:" RESULT

  /* Number of open windows */
  'GETATTR WINDOWS.COUNT'
  SAY "Open windows:" RESULT

  /* Active window */
  'GETATTR WINDOWS.ACTIVE'
  SAY "Active:" RESULT

  /* Window position */
  'GETATTR WINDOW.LEFT NAME "Work:"'
  SAY "Left:" RESULT

  /* List all windows */
  'GETATTR WINDOWS.COUNT'
  count = RESULT
  DO i = 0 TO count - 1
      'GETATTR WINDOWS.'i
      SAY "Window:" RESULT
  END

  /* All icons in root window */
  'GETATTR WINDOW.ICONS.ALL.COUNT NAME ROOT'
  count = RESULT
  DO i = 0 TO count - 1
      'GETATTR WINDOW.ICONS.ALL.'i'.NAME NAME ROOT'
      SAY "Icon:" RESULT
  END

## FAULT

Returns a human-readable error message for an AmigaDOS error code.

Syntax: FAULT CODE/A/N

Parameters:
  CODE/A/N    AmigaDOS error code (required, numeric)

Return: RESULT contains the error description.

Examples:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'FAULT 205'
  SAY RESULT   /* "Object not found" */

  'FAULT 221'
  SAY RESULT   /* "Disk is full" */

## HELP

Displays help information about Workbench ARexx commands.

Syntax: HELP [COMMAND/K] [MENUS/S] [PROMPT/S]

Parameters:
  COMMAND/K    Show syntax of a specific command
  MENUS/S      List available menu items
  PROMPT/S     Invoke the help system

Return: RESULT contains the help text.

Examples:
  OPTIONS RESULTS
  'HELP COMMAND GETATTR'
  SAY RESULT

  'HELP MENUS'
  SAY RESULT

## MENU

Invokes standard menu items or creates/removes custom menu entries.

Syntax: MENU [WINDOW/K] [INVOKE] [NAME/K] [TITLE/K] [SHORTCUT/K]
             [ADD/S] [REMOVE/S] [CMD/K/F]

Parameters:
  WINDOW/K     Target window (for window-specific menu items)
  INVOKE       Execute the named menu item
  NAME/K       Unique identifier for the menu item
  TITLE/K      Display text for custom menu items
  SHORTCUT/K   Keyboard shortcut (one character)
  ADD/S        Add a custom menu item
  REMOVE/S     Remove a custom menu item
  CMD/K/F      ARexx command to execute when item is selected

Standard Menu Items:
  Workbench menu:
    WORKBENCH.BACKDROP       Toggle backdrop mode
    WORKBENCH.EXECUTE        Execute command dialog
    WORKBENCH.REDRAWALL      Redraw all windows
    WORKBENCH.UPDATEALL      Update all windows
    WORKBENCH.LASTMESSAGE    Show last error message
    WORKBENCH.ABOUT          About Workbench dialog
    WORKBENCH.QUIT           Quit Workbench

  Window menu:
    WINDOW.NEWDRAWER         Create new drawer
    WINDOW.OPENPARENT        Open parent directory
    WINDOW.CLOSE             Close window
    WINDOW.UPDATE            Update window contents
    WINDOW.SELECTCONTENTS    Select all icons
    WINDOW.CLEARSELECTION    Clear selection
    WINDOW.RESIZETOFIT       Resize window to fit contents
    WINDOW.SNAPSHOT.WINDOW   Snapshot window position
    WINDOW.SNAPSHOT.ALL      Snapshot window and all icons
    WINDOW.SHOW.ONLYICONS    Show only icons
    WINDOW.SHOW.ALLFILES     Show all files

  Cleanup:
    WINDOW.CLEANUPBY.COLUMN  Clean up in columns
    WINDOW.CLEANUPBY.NAME    Clean up by name
    WINDOW.CLEANUPBY.DATE    Clean up by date
    WINDOW.CLEANUPBY.SIZE    Clean up by size
    WINDOW.CLEANUPBY.TYPE    Clean up by type

  View:
    WINDOW.VIEWBY.ICON       View as icons
    WINDOW.VIEWBY.NAME       View by name (list)
    WINDOW.VIEWBY.DATE       View by date (list)
    WINDOW.VIEWBY.SIZE       View by size (list)
    WINDOW.VIEWBY.TYPE       View by type (list)

  Icons menu:
    ICONS.OPEN               Open selected icons
    ICONS.COPY               Copy selected icons
    ICONS.RENAME             Rename selected icon
    ICONS.INFORMATION        Show icon information
    ICONS.SNAPSHOT           Save icon position
    ICONS.UNSNAPSHOT         Remove saved position
    ICONS.LEAVEOUT           Leave out on Workbench
    ICONS.PUTAWAY            Put away (undo leave out)
    ICONS.DELETE             Delete selected icons
    ICONS.FORMATDISK         Format disk
    ICONS.EMPTYTRASH         Empty trashcan

  Tools menu:
    TOOLS.RESETWB            Reset Workbench

Examples:
  /* Invoke standard menu items */
  'MENU INVOKE WORKBENCH.ABOUT'
  'MENU WINDOW "Work:" INVOKE WINDOW.CLEANUPBY.NAME'

  /* Add custom menu item */
  'MENU ADD NAME "MyTool" TITLE "My Tool" SHORTCUT "M" CMD "rx MyScript.rexx"'

  /* Remove custom menu item */
  'MENU REMOVE NAME "MyTool"'

## KEYBOARD

Binds ARexx commands to keyboard shortcuts using the Commodities
input event format.

Syntax: KEYBOARD NAME/A [ADD/S] [REMOVE/S] [KEY] [CMD/F]

Parameters:
  NAME/A      Unique identifier for the binding (required)
  ADD/S       Add a new keyboard binding
  REMOVE/S    Remove an existing binding
  KEY         Key combination in Commodities format
              e.g. "ctrl a", "alt f1", "shift ctrl q"
  CMD/F       ARexx script or command to execute

Examples:
  /* Bind Ctrl+A to a script */
  'KEYBOARD ADD NAME "MyHotkey" KEY "ctrl a" CMD "rx MyScript.rexx"'

  /* Remove binding */
  'KEYBOARD REMOVE NAME "MyHotkey"'

  /* Bind Alt+F1 */
  'KEYBOARD ADD NAME "ShowInfo" KEY "alt f1" CMD "rx ShowInfo.rexx"'

## RX

Executes ARexx scripts and commands.

Syntax: RX [CONSOLE/S] [ASYNC/S] CMD/A/F

Parameters:
  CONSOLE/S    Open a console window for I/O
  ASYNC/S      Execute asynchronously (don't wait for completion)
  CMD/A/F      Script filename or inline ARexx command (required)

Examples:
  'RX CMD "test.wb"'
  'RX ASYNC CMD "long_script.rexx"'
  'RX CONSOLE CMD "interactive.rexx"'
